# Apex — HTTP Callout Pattern

## Standard pattern

```java
private static MyResponseType callExternalApi(String recordId, MyConfig__mdt config) {
    Integer timeoutMs = config.Callout_Timeout_Ms__c != null
        ? config.Callout_Timeout_Ms__c.intValue()
        : 10000;

    // URL-encode any dynamic query parameters
    String filters = EncodingUtil.urlEncode('[["field","=","value"]]', 'UTF-8');

    HttpRequest req = new HttpRequest();
    req.setEndpoint(config.Endpoint__c + '/api/resource/MyDoc?filters=' + filters);
    req.setMethod('GET');
    req.setHeader('Authorization', 'Bearer ' + getAccessToken(config));
    req.setHeader('Accept', 'application/json');
    req.setTimeout(timeoutMs);

    HttpResponse res = new Http().send(req);

    if (res.getStatusCode() != 200) {
        throw new CalloutException('API returned HTTP '
            + res.getStatusCode() + ': ' + res.getBody());
    }

    Map<String, Object> parsed = (Map<String, Object>) JSON.deserializeUntyped(res.getBody());
    // Access response fields: parsed.get('data'), etc.
    return buildResult(parsed);
}
```

## Caller always wraps in try/catch

```java
MyResponseType result;
try {
    result = callExternalApi(recordId, config);
} catch (Exception ex) {
    System.debug('Callout failed: ' + ex.getMessage());
    result = buildFallbackResult();  // never leave result null
}
```

## Key rules

- Always set a timeout — default Salesforce timeout is 10s but external APIs can be slow; read from Custom Metadata so it's configurable without a deploy
- Always URL-encode filter strings — special characters in query params silently corrupt the request
- Use `JSON.deserializeUntyped` → `Map<String, Object>` for parsing external API responses; typed deserialization breaks on unexpected or missing fields
- Throw `CalloutException` (not a custom exception) on non-200 — callers can catch `Exception` generically and handle fallback
- Named Credential or Custom Metadata for endpoint + credentials — never hardcode URLs or tokens in Apex

## POST with JSON body

```java
HttpRequest req = new HttpRequest();
req.setEndpoint(config.Endpoint__c + '/api/resource/Purchase%20Order');
req.setMethod('POST');
req.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
req.setHeader('Accept', 'application/json');
req.setHeader('Authorization', 'Bearer ' + getAccessToken(config));
req.setBody(JSON.serialize(bodyMap));
req.setTimeout(timeoutMs);
```
